  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. 📋 Executive Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Problem\n",
    "Olist is Brazil's largest online marketplace aggregator, connecting thousands of sellers to customers across the country. Despite strong order volume growth, the platform faces a critical challenge: **understanding what drives poor customer experiences and where the business must focus to sustain growth and satisfaction**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dataset\n",
    "- **~100,000 orders** from 2016–2018 across 9 relational tables\n",
    "- Covers orders, payments, reviews, customers, sellers, products, and geography\n",
    "\n",
    "### Analytical Approach\n",
    "Every analysis follows: **Business Question → Data Preparation → Analysis → Visualization → Finding → Recommendation**\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🔑 Most Important Findings (Real Numbers)\n",
    "1. **Late deliveries devastate ratings** — Late orders average **2.26/5** vs **4.28/5** for early deliveries\n",
    "2. **32.44% of low-review orders are late** — but only 2.91% of high-review orders are late\n",
    "3. **SP and RJ dominate volume** but RJ has 12.1% late delivery rate vs SP's 4.5%\n",
    "4. **6.78% of delivered orders arrive late** — impacting ~6,500 customers\n",
    "5. **Office furniture, audio, and home comfort categories** have the lowest satisfaction scores\n",
    "6. **96% of customers never return** — massive repeat-purchase opportunity is being missed\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🎯 Key Recommendations\n",
    "1. Launch a late-delivery early-warning system targeting high-risk routes\n",
    "2. Implement seller accountability scoring with minimum performance thresholds\n",
    "3. Create a post-delivery win-back program for customers who experienced delays\n",
    "4. Invest in logistics infrastructure in RJ, AM, and AL (highest late rates)\n",
    "5. Audit quality and logistics for low-satisfaction categories"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. 🏢 Business Problem\n",
    "\n",
    "Olist operates as a marketplace connector — it does not directly ship products. Instead, it enables thousands of independent sellers to list products and fulfill orders through Brazil's logistics network.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why customer experience matters for a marketplace:**\n",
    "- Reviews directly affect seller and platform reputation\n",
    "- Delivery performance is the #1 post-purchase touchpoint Olist can influence\n",
    "- Geographic spread across Brazil creates massive logistics complexity\n",
    "- Category diversity means quality risks vary by product type\n",
    "- Payment flexibility (installments) signals price sensitivity in a developing market\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key business questions this project answers:**\n",
    "1. Is the marketplace growing? Are there growth or decline inflection points?\n",
    "2. What percentage of orders are late, and how does that affect ratings?\n",
    "3. Which states/regions have the worst delivery performance?\n",
    "4. Which sellers need intervention?\n",
    "5. Which product categories are dragging down satisfaction?\n",
    "6. What factors are most strongly associated with 1-2 star reviews?\n",
    "7. What can Olist do to measurably improve customer experience?"
   ]
  },
  {
