    "## 14. 🎯 Key Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Finding 1: Late Deliveries Are the Primary Driver of Low Satisfaction\n",
    "**Evidence:** Late orders average **2.26/5** stars vs **4.28/5** for early orders — a gap of 2.02 points. Among low-review orders (≤2 stars), **32.44% involve late delivery**, compared to only **2.91%** among high-review orders — a **11x difference**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business Impact:** Delivery reliability is the single most controllable factor affecting customer experience on the platform. With 6,542 late orders, each delay is a direct risk to a 1-2 star review.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recommendation:** Implement a real-time delivery risk scoring system. Flag orders predicted to be late by Day 5 post-purchase. Trigger proactive customer communication and expedite carrier escalation.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Finding 2: RJ (Rio de Janeiro) is a High-Risk Delivery State\n",
    "**Evidence:** RJ has a **12.1% late delivery rate** — nearly 3x higher than SP's 4.5%. RJ is the 2nd largest state by order volume (12,350 orders) and has an average review score of **3.95**, below the platform average of 4.07.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business Impact:** With 12,350 orders, even a 2% improvement in RJ's late rate would protect ~250 customer experiences per period.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recommendation:** Audit last-mile logistics partners operating in RJ. Negotiate SLA improvements or add carrier redundancy. Consider a dedicated logistics review for RJ routes.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Finding 3: 96.9% of Customers Never Return\n",
    "**Evidence:** Of 96,096 unique customers, only **2,997 (3.1%)** placed more than one order on the platform. The median customer made exactly one purchase. The maximum order count for any single customer was 17.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business Impact:** Olist is operating primarily as a single-purchase acquisition machine. CLV (Customer Lifetime Value) is severely constrained. Each poor experience permanently loses that customer.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recommendation:** Launch a post-delivery email sequence targeting customers with scores ≥4. Offer personalized category recommendations and loyalty incentives within 14 days of delivery.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Finding 4: High Freight-to-Value Ratio is Associated with Lower Satisfaction\n",
    "**Evidence:** Low-review orders average **R$27.74 in freight** vs **R$22.04** for high-review orders — a 26% premium. Orders where freight exceeds 30% of product value show meaningfully lower review scores.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business Impact:** Customers notice when shipping costs approach or exceed product value. This may signal both logistics inefficiency and product pricing perception issues.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recommendation:** Set freight cost thresholds per category. Work with sellers to enable minimum product price floors in high-freight categories. Explore regional fulfillment partnerships.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Finding 5: Office Furniture and Audio Categories Have Critically Low Satisfaction\n",
    "**Evidence:** Office furniture averages **3.48/5**, audio **3.81/5**, and home comfort **3.83/5** — all substantially below the platform average of 4.07. Audio also has an **11.5% late delivery rate** — among the highest of all categories.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business Impact:** These categories carry both quality perception and logistics risk. Continued poor performance will drag overall platform ratings.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recommendation:** Conduct seller-level quality audits in these categories. Implement mandatory seller performance reviews if average score remains below 3.7 for 60 days.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Finding 6: Marketplace Showed Strong Growth to Mid-2018, Then Plateaued\n",
    "**Evidence:** Monthly orders grew from near-zero in late 2016 to a peak of **7,289 orders** in the highest-volume month, driven primarily by 2017–2018 growth. Late 2018 data shows signs of plateauing. Revenue tracked order volume growth, with peak monthly revenue of **R$987,765**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business Impact:** Without intervention on retention and satisfaction, growth from new customer acquisition alone may not sustain revenue momentum.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recommendation:** Shift marketing investment mix toward retention and re-engagement. A 5% improvement in repeat purchase rate could add thousands of orders annually without incremental CAC.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Finding 7: Credit Card Dominates Payments but Voucher Users Show Lower Satisfaction\n",
    "**Evidence:** Credit cards account for **76.1%** of orders with an average value of **R$166.57**. Voucher users show the lowest average review score at **3.94** (vs platform avg 4.07). This association does not imply causation — voucher users may disproportionately represent disappointed or first-time buyers.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business Impact:** Understanding voucher usage patterns can help identify friction points in the promotional purchase funnel.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recommendation:** Analyze voucher user journeys separately. If vouchers are primarily used for recovery from a previous bad experience, the satisfaction signal is a recovery effectiveness metric, not a payment method effect."
